title: Cloudflare
agents: cloudflare
catalog: cloud/cloudflare
license: WTFPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors Cloudflare resources including:

 - Workers: Script analytics (requests, errors, CPU time P50/P99)
 - KV Namespaces: Operations (reads, writes, deletes, lists), key count
 - DNS Zones: Zone status (active/paused)
 - R2 Buckets: Bucket location and status
 - Zone Analytics: HTTP requests, bandwidth, threats, cache hit ratio
 - DNS Analytics: Query count, response time, response codes
 - WAF Events: Security events (blocked, challenged)
 - Page Rules: Rule count and status
 - Cloudflare Access: Applications and policies
 - Cloudflare Tunnel: Tunnel status and connections
 - Load Balancers: Pool health and origin status

 The check uses the Cloudflare REST API and GraphQL API to retrieve
 current status data and analytics for all configured services.

 Configuration options in WATO:
 - API Token: Cloudflare API authentication
 - Account ID: Your Cloudflare account identifier
 - Services: Select which services to monitor
 - Cache TTL: Metrics cache duration (default: 300s)
 - Discovery TTL: Resource discovery cache duration (default: 3600s)
 - Analytics Timeframe: 5m, 15m, 1h, 6h, or 24h

discovery:
 One service is created for each discovered Cloudflare resource
 (Worker, KV Namespace, Zone, R2 Bucket, Access App, Tunnel, LB Pool).
 Additionally, an API Usage service tracks API calls made by the agent.
